 "about": "Attic cartouche of the Garden Gate (plate 4, 'North Side of Garden Gate'), left half, drawn by hand as smooth curves while viewing the University of Manchester copy of the 1786 engravings online (PR-CHCR-00457, image 26). Only these hand-drawn control points are used; no pixels of that scan. Coordinates are that scan's pixels. Curves are Catmull-Rom splines through the points. The right half is the mirror image. the cartouche's body (its members closed up by plinth_close album px) stands at plinth_level; the closed members and bands rise from it, and the lines inside them are grooves. Manchester x 3983 is the centre of the shield's top bar and of its sides, but the album's cartouche is about 5 Manchester px narrower each side of its axis (fitting both album halves to the mirrored drawing puts the axis at 3978, scale 0.64, y unchanged), so the drawing maps from x 3978; members that sit on the axis (finial, axis stems, ring and bead) were moved 5 px left with it to keep their traced width. y 2129 is the attic volute eye's height, album 2482/1296.",
